# Wireframe: NotFoundPage

## Purpose & Flow Context

Displayed when the user navigates to a URL that does not match any registered route. Serves the 404 Handling flow. Entry: any unmatched URL. Exit: user clicks "Go to Dashboard" link → navigates to `/`.

---

## Notation Legend

| Symbol | Meaning | Symbol | Meaning |
|--------|---------|--------|---------|
| `[...]` | Button / interactive element | `[>...▼]` | Dropdown |
| `_______` | Text input / editable field | `[X]` | Close / dismiss |
| `⚠` | Warning / due date | `📎N` | N attachments |
| `💬N` | N comments | `🔗` | Card relationship |
| `👤` | User / mention | `○ ●` | Radio unselected / selected |

## Accessibility — Shared Conventions

All interactive screens inherit these. Per-screen specifics noted where they diverge.

| Concern | Convention |
|---------|------------|
| Landmarks | `header`, `main`, `aside`, `contentinfo` |
| Heading order | One `h1` per screen, `h2` for sections |
| Accessible names | Icon-only controls get `aria-label` |
| Keyboard | Tab, Enter/Space, Escape, Arrow keys |
| Target size | ≥24×24 CSS px reservation |
| Non-color intent | Icon + text, never color alone |

---

## Layout Regions

**Grid**: Single-column centred layout. Spacing cadence: 8px rhythm intent.

**App-shell**: Rendered without sidebar/header — standalone page (public, no auth required).

| Region | Content | Notes |
|--------|---------|-------|
| Main | Centred container in `<main>` | Fills viewport height with flex centring |
| Status icon | Large 404 graphic or icon | Optional illustration above heading |
| Heading | `<h1>` "Page not found" | Main heading, focus target on mount |
| Message | `<p>` descriptive text | Explains the situation in plain language |
| Action link | RouteLink "Go to Dashboard" | Programmatic navigation to `/` |

**Content hierarchy** (by visual priority):
1. Status icon — immediate visual signal
2. Heading — clearly states the problem
3. Message — optional context
4. Action link — recovery path

```
+------------------------------------------------------------------+
|                                                                    |
|                                                                    |
|                       [ 404 Illustration ]                         |
|                                                                    |
|                    # Page not found                                |
|                                                                    |
|            The page you're looking for doesn't exist.              |
|                                                                    |
|              [Go to Dashboard]                                     |
|                                                                    |
|                                                                    |
+------------------------------------------------------------------+
```

*Legend: [{Button}] [Input] [Link] [#Heading] [>Dropdown] [Avatar] [Icon]*

## Components & Affordances

| Element | DS Component | Behavior | Edge Cases |
|---------|-------------|----------|------------|
| 404 illustration | — (custom SVG/icon) | Static display, decorative | `aria-hidden="true"` |
| Heading | — (HTML `<h1>`) | Static text | Focus target on mount via `tabindex="-1"` |
| Message | — (HTML `<p>`) | Static text | — |
| "Go to Dashboard" link | RouteLink (RouteLink variant) | Click → navigate to `/` | Auth guard applies after navigation |

## Data Display

N/A — static content page.

## Content & Microcopy Intent

| Slot | Intent | Notes |
|------|--------|-------|
| 404 illustration | Visual cue that page is missing | Decorative, not relied upon for meaning |
| "Page not found" | Clear, direct problem statement | User language — no technical "404" code as primary message |
| "The page you're looking for doesn't exist." | Plain-language explanation | Avoids jargon |
| "Go to Dashboard" | Primary recovery action | Links to `/`; if unauthenticated, auth guard handles redirect |

## States

### Populated (Default)

The single state of this screen — always the same content regardless of how user arrived.

```
+------------------------------------------------------------------+
|                                                                    |
|                       [ 404 Illustration ]                         |
|                                                                    |
|                    # Page not found                                |
|                                                                    |
|            The page you're looking for doesn't exist.              |
|                                                                    |
|              [Go to Dashboard]                                     |
|                                                                    |
+------------------------------------------------------------------+
```

### Loading

N/A — static page with no data fetching.

### Empty

N/A — no data to be empty.

### Error

N/A — the page itself is the error state.

## Responsive

| Breakpoint | Changes |
|------------|---------|
| Desktop (>1024px) | Full-size illustration, centred layout |
| Tablet (768-1024px) | Illustration may scale down, layout remains centred |
| Mobile (<768px) | Illustration hidden or reduced, heading and link remain, 16px padding on each side |

## Accessibility — Screen Composition

| Concern | Implementation |
|---------|----------------|
| Landmarks | `<main>` with `role="alert"` announces the page type on mount |
| Heading order | Single `<h1>` — "Page not found" |
| Reading / Focus order | Focus moved to `<h1>` on page mount via `tabindex="-1"` |
| Accessible names | Decorative illustration gets `aria-hidden="true"`, no label needed |
| Keyboard operability | Tab to "Go to Dashboard" link, Enter to navigate |
| Target size | RouteLink inline — ensure ≥24×24 CSS px clickable area |
| Focus not obscured | No sticky regions on this page |
| Non-color intent | Text + heading convey meaning, not colour |

*Defer to design-system: pixel contrast, focus-appearance, per-component target-size/keyboard.*
